@startuml paradigm-detection
' The analyze_tokens dataflow: token stream → indexed pattern probe → literal
' match → confidence → weighted accumulation → density normalisation → profile.
' Colour encodes stage role: code/token artifacts (orange), analysis (purple),
' scoring arithmetic (indigo), output (green), configuration inputs (slate).
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/paradigm-detection.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/paradigm/detection.md §3
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title ParadigmDetector::analyze_tokens — probe → match → weigh → accumulate → normalise

rectangle "**Input**\n\"class Foo extends Bar { this.x = 0; }\"" as in #455A64
rectangle "**0. tokenize()**\nalphanumeric+_ runs kept whole;\nevery other non-space char\nbecomes its own token\n[class · Foo · extends · Bar · { · this · . · x · = · 0 · ; · } ]" as tok #EF6C00

rectangle "**1. pattern_index probe**\nHashMap<String, Vec<(Paradigm, usize)>>\nkeyed on each pattern's FIRST token —\nO(1) per token, no scan of 170 patterns" as idx #6A1B9A
rectangle "**2. try_match()**\nlower-case literal comparison of the\nwhole token sequence  s(π)\n(only 1 of 170 patterns is multi-token)" as mat #7B1FA2
rectangle "**3. calculate_confidence()**\nconf = min(1, κ + 0.1·b·σ)\nκ = 1 when no context is required,\nelse the fraction of required context\ntokens present in the ±ω window" as conf #8E24AA

rectangle "**4. accumulate**\nS(p) += w(π) · conf · μ(p)\nw ∈ {0.9 strong, 0.6 medium, 0.3 weak}\nμ(p) = the paradigm's multiplier" as acc #283593
rectangle "**5. density normalise**  (normalize_scores)\nŜ(p) = min(1, S(p) · 100 / max(n,1))\n— a score *per 100 tokens*, capped at 1;\nNOT a sum-to-one normalisation" as norm #303F9F

rectangle "**ParadigmProfile**\noop 0.72 · fp 0.05 · reactive 0.00 · procedural 0.31\nindicators · match_count · total_tokens" as prof #2E7D32
rectangle "**DetectionResult**\nprofile + matches (with context)\n+ stats (tokens, checks, time_us)" as res #2E7D32

rectangle "**ParadigmConfig**\ncontext_window ω\nweights.strong_indicator_bonus b\nweights.*_multiplier μ\nnormalize_scores" as cfg #546E7A

in --> tok
tok --> idx : per token tᵢ
idx --> mat : candidate patterns
mat --> conf : on match
conf --> acc
acc --> norm : after all tokens
norm --> prof
prof --> res

cfg -[#546E7A]-> conf
cfg -[#546E7A]-> acc
cfg -[#546E7A]-> norm

note right of idx
  The index is the reason detection is
  **O(n · k)**, not O(n · |Π|): only the
  k patterns sharing the current token's
  first token are ever tested.
end note

note right of norm
  The cap makes Ŝ **saturating**: once a
  paradigm exceeds 1 match-weight per
  100 tokens its score pins at 1.0, so
  dominance compares //saturated// scores.
end note
@enduml
